{"causes": ["The systematic persecution of Christians by Roman emperors like Diocletian and Licinius created a climate where steadfast faith often led to martyrdom.", "The rising influence and spread of Christianity within the Roman Empire presented a direct challenge to traditional Roman polytheism and imperial authority.", "The inherent conflict between military duty requiring loyalty to the emperor and the Christian prohibition against idol worship frequently placed Christian soldiers in an untenable position."], "effects": ["The martyrdom of Theodore Stratelates solidified his status as a powerful intercessor and patron saint for soldiers and those facing persecution.", "His story contributed significantly to the rich hagiographic tradition of warrior saints, inspiring countless believers and shaping Christian ideals of courage.", "The widespread veneration of Theodore Stratelates led to the construction of numerous churches and monasteries dedicated to him across the Byzantine world."], "relationships": [{"sourceSlug": "licinius", "sourceName": "Licinius", "verb": "CAUSES", "targetSlug": "theodore-stratelates", "targetName": "Theodore Stratelates", "context": "Emperor Licinius's renewed persecution of Christians directly led to the arrest and martyrdom of Theodore Stratelates in 319 CE."}, {"sourceSlug": "theodore-stratelates", "sourceName": "Theodore Stratelates", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "byzantine-art", "targetName": "Byzantine Art", "context": "Theodore Stratelates's iconic image as a mounted warrior saint became a recurring and significant motif in Byzantine iconography and art."}, {"sourceSlug": "theodore-stratelates", "sourceName": "Theodore Stratelates", "verb": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "heraclea-pontica", "targetName": "Heraclea Pontica", "context": "The martyrdom of Theodore Stratelates is traditionally believed to have occurred in Heraclea Pontica, a city in ancient Bithynia."}, {"sourceSlug": "early-christian-martyrdom", "sourceName": "